# WolkaraForever layer patch 0905 - Battery Saver 40 FPS pacing and a refresh-rate log (personal branch)
#
# Why: the owner of this branch wants the game allowed 120 Hz on an iPhone Duo, with the game's
# own Max Foreground FPS as the limit, and Battery Saver offering 60, 40 or 30. Without
# CADisableMinimumFrameDurationOnPhone iOS shows an iPhone app on a 60 Hz rhythm, and the
# game's own 40 FPS cap was seen on the Duo alternating short and long frames. This branch adds
# the opt-in to the app's Info.plist and a Battery Saver 40 (BatterySaverPolicy). Upstream keeps
# 60 Hz on purpose, for heat, so this is a personal test, not an upstream candidate.
#
# What it changes in the Metal adapter:
#   - The hold. A capped frame is held 2 ms less than the cap's interval: exactly the interval
#     sits on a refresh boundary (25 ms is three 120 Hz refreshes), and on the Duo whole seconds
#     of a 40 cap came out at 33.3 ms with the screen at 120 Hz. 2 ms keeps the intended refresh
#     count at every rate the policy uses. A game's own longer duration is still kept.
#   - Timed presentation under a cap. When the cap, not the game's own time, decides when a
#     frame may appear, the frame is presented with a minimum duration instead of at a host
#     time. A host time lands on whichever refresh follows it, so 25 ms targets on a 60 Hz
#     rhythm alternate 16.7 and 33.3 ms; a minimum duration rounds up to whole refreshes - a
#     steady 40 at 120 Hz, and a steady 30 when 120 Hz is not available. The simulator, which
#     has no minimum-duration presentation, keeps the timed target.
#   - Measurement. In an app with the opt-in, every session records presented frames for its
#     whole run (closing the HUD does not stop it) and counts how long each stayed on screen,
#     in the refresh multiples a ProMotion iPhone can show. DisplayRate.m logs and clears the
#     counts once a second. Without the opt-in nothing here changes.
#
# Applies after: 0904-large-phone-screen-holds-landscape.patch
# Applies to: translation/Metal/Presentation.m
# Upstream: no (personal branch).
#
--- a/translation/Metal/Presentation.m
+++ b/translation/Metal/Presentation.m
